            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "JWQYN",
              "name": "Contract Columns",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": 350,
              "gap": 16,
              "padding": 20,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "ZMVRK",
                  "name": "Ordered Real-UI Scenario Steps",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": "fill_container",
                  "fill": "$panelAlt",
                  "cornerRadius": 12,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 10,
                  "padding": 16,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "WjZI2",
                      "name": "Scenario Steps Label",
                      "fill": "$blue",
                      "content": "01 · ORDERED REAL-UI STEPS",
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "800",
                      "letterSpacing": 0.7
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Q6saU",
                      "name": "Scenario Steps Content",
                      "fill": "$text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "1. Create Tab A and enter the complete GET request through rendered controls.\n\n2. Click New Request and build the distinguishable POST JSON request in Tab B.\n\n3. Switch with mouse click, then focus each tab and press Enter / Space; both paths run one activation command.\n\n4. Every switch restores the owning Method, URL, Params, Headers, Auth, Body, pane, response, and dirty state.\n\n5. Send Tab A and Tab B directly without Enter, Tab, blur, Add, or submit-time backfill.\n\n6. Close Tab B; Tab A becomes the valid active tab and shared History retains both completed Requests.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3,
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "g8UNbw",
                  "name": "Observable Assertions · Verification Contract",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": "fill_container",
                  "fill": "$blueSoft",
                  "cornerRadius": 12,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 10,
                  "padding": 16,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "IUmL5",
                      "name": "Observable Assertions Label",
                      "fill": "$blue",
                      "content": "02 · OBSERVABLE ASSERTIONS",
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "800",
                      "letterSpacing": 0.7
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "XbGAA",
                      "name": "Observable Assertions Content",
                      "fill": "$text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "• Tab A sends GET /get?tab=A&q=rust with X-Tab: A, no Auth, and RequestBody::None.\n\n• Tab B sends POST /anything/tab-b?mode=json with X-Tab: B, Bearer auth, and typed JSON.\n\n• Each HTTPBingo echo and ResponseState remains attached to its originating tab_id.\n\n• Switching projects state; controls retain no cross-tab business model and perform no copying between ViewModels.\n\n• dirty=true remains on the unsent owner; successful Send clears only that owner to dirty=false.\n\n• Runtime History records exactly two completed Requests; closing a tab changes no record. Restart restores durable sanitized History only, never tabs.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3,
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "nkQPy",
                  "name": "Scope and Non-Goals",
                  "width": "fill_container",
